# Chapter 10, Section 28: "What Does It Matter Now?"



――The "Sword Saint."

――The "Blue Lightning."

――The "Admirer."

――The "Mad Prince."


These were all titles bestowed upon the strongest beings in this world.

The Kingdom of Lugunica, the Vollachia Empire, the Kararagi City-States, the Gusteko Holy Kingdom――these were existences praised as the strongest in each of the four great nations, transcendents who had reached strengths beyond human comprehension.


However, as was widely known, even among them, the one known for standing head and shoulders above the rest was the current "Sword Saint," the strongest existence on earth――Reinhard Van Astrea.


Looking across past, present, and future, Reinhard's existence was evaluated as one that would likely never see a superior life form born again. He didn't even fit within the framework of the four great nations' strongest.

But precisely because of that, there was a fact quietly overlooked.――It was the fact that, hidden by the irregular existence that was Reinhard, the glorious name of a warrior who would normally have been worthy of being mentioned alongside the other three was being severely underestimated.


The strongest "Sword Saint" in history――the person who could only be contained within the shadow of that glory, that was――




"――Marcos."


With a hoarse, feeble voice, Heinkel's lips called that man's name.

Heinkel, who was on the taller side himself, was faced with a large man a full head taller than him, who lightly pressed down on his drawn sword with a palm the size of a child's head.

What was terrifying was that this wasn't mere physical strength. When he tried to draw, it pressed down; when he tried to lower it, it pushed back. The hilt and scabbard remained perfectly flush, with not a sliver of the blade visible.


As if to demonstrate that this was the difference in caliber between Marcos, the Captain of the Royal Guard, and Heinkel, who had been seated in the decorative position of Vice Captain.


"――Release your hand from the sword, Heinkel."


A deep voice that made one's guts tremble echoed through the corridor.

A physique approaching two meters, thick muscles befitting that massive frame, and a trained body wrapped in silver full-body armor――the figure stood in stillness yet exuded an undeniable sword spirit and overwhelming presence that made him seem larger than he was, praised as being more giant-like than a giant himself.


Marcos Gildark――Captain of the Kingdom of Lugunica's Royal Guard, a formidable warrior known by the epithet "The Boulder."

From his youth when he was a mere knight in the order, he was a man who had made even the "Sword Demon" Wilhelm Van Astrea declare that the position of future Knight Captain was certainly his.


"――gh"


In an instant, cold sweat covered Heinkel's entire body.

His back became soaked, and greasy sweat burst forth on his face and neck. Cold sweat for fear, greasy sweat as the alarm of survival instinct――he found himself admiring how his own body had such dexterous ways of being afraid.


"Lady Felt, Lady Philoane, please step away from this man."


Once again, while Heinkel committed the folly of being dominated by his habitual misplaced thoughts, Marcos cast a sharp glance toward the depths of the passageway――toward the two peering from the stairs.

At that instruction, there was the sound of Philoane and Felt catching their breath,


"W-Wait, Knight Captain! Sir Heinkel is..."


"――Shut up!!"


"Eh!?"


In an instant, Philoane, who had opened her mouth toward Marcos, was silenced by Heinkel's angry shout. But the voice that tried to perform violent rage cracked, and the end of the words trailed off pathetically.

He had no composure to turn around. But he could see it clearly in his mind's eye――Philoane, her red eyes round with shock, staring frozen at his back.


His chest ached. But this was necessary. Silencing her was.

If it was now, still――,


"Just when I thought you'd neatly settled into the position of Lady Philoane's knight, you infiltrate the royal castle aiming to seize Lady Felt and Lady Emilia.――Who put you up to this, 'Sword-Bearer'?"


Feeling the undisguised disgust and contempt in that voice suppressing emotion, Heinkel twisted his cheek in self-deprecation.――Yes, if it was now, it could still be made into that.

That everything was Heinkel's scheme, that Philoane had been used by him, that Felt too had merely been forcibly taken along, and that neither held any rebellious intent toward the royal castle or the "Dragon God Church."

So that such an excuse would hold, he had kept Philoane uninvolved in the plan's preparations for these past two weeks.


Of course, it was insurance that would best go unused. However, the application of that insurance was now confirmed.――He had encountered Marcos.

Against an opponent he could absolutely never defeat, no matter if he had a hundred, a thousand, or ten thousand chances to challenge――he had been found.


"Old man..."


Beside Philoane, silenced by the angry shout, Felt murmured quietly.

The tone of her voice was surely evidence that she had sensed the meaning of Heinkel's insurance. What a perceptive girl. Probably not of Lugunican royal blood. Philoane, with her resigned yet stubbornly breathing manner, had more convincing credentials as a member of that good-natured family.

On top of that――,


"Having abandoned your duties as Vice Captain, drowned yourself in drink, and continued to make your son clean up the messes of your own failures――what do you scheme now, dragging in royal selection candidates?――Answer me."


"――――"


"Answer me, Heinkel. Show some knightly quality for once in your life."


At those words, Heinkel's vision flashed crimson.

"Knightly quality for once"――to be told that by a man blessed with the power to behave knightly, blessed with the opportunities, blessed with bravery, made a thick black impulse well up from the depths of his heart.

Marcos should know.

What Heinkel had lost, what he had thrown away, what it had all been for. Knowing that, what right did he have to condemn Heinkel, still struggling and flailing?


"Don't spout your whining, Heinkel."


"――ah"

"A great many people, like you, face adversity and yet hold their heads high without breaking. Though born into a position more blessed than any of them, you ruined even that through your own actions.――Who could possibly sympathize with you?"


He couldn't speak. Nothing at all.

Neither shouting nor spitting out, that flat voice deeply gouged Heinkel's vitals. With his vitals so gouged, Heinkel bit the inside of his cheek and raised his face through the pain.

Marcos's frozen eyes, close before him――he glared straight into them and opened his mouth.

To speak the villainous words befitting the application of his prepared insurance――,


"――hyu"


But from his constricted throat, not even the single word "that's right" that he needed to say came out.


"――. You truly never grow at all, do you."


It was a single phrase, like a sigh, that could have been either disappointment or dejection.

However, the mighty fist that followed that phrase ignored all the quiet exchange up to that point, struck Heinkel's temple, and slammed him into the stone wall as it was.


"ka"


The stone wall caved in from that single blow, and radial cracks ran like lightning through the floor and ceiling. The muffled cry of pain was swallowed by the sound of destruction, and stone fragments rained down upon Heinkel's head as he collapsed.


He'd been struck. That was all.

Without even properly taking a stance, a single blow with a gesture like brushing aside something in the way――that alone sent Heinkel's body flying like a thin broken branch.

Heinkel, who had been forced to face a "Dragon" in the Vollachia Empire in unwelcome circumstances, felt the same oppressive pressure from Marcos as he had from that "Dragon"――clearly, it was the feeling of facing a life form of an entirely different foundation.


"Sir Heinkel!!"


A voice like a scream――Philoane's cry was distant.

Amidst the crumbled stone fragments, he tried to push himself up with his hands. But the hand that should have touched the floor slipped, and Heinkel fell face-first into the rubble disgracefully.

Intense pain ran through his nose, and blood dripped. As that blood entered his throat and made him cough, a merciless toe kicked through Heinkel's chin.


"Ga――!?"


His face kicked upward, Heinkel's body flew straight up and crashed into the ceiling.

His body, nearly embedded in the ceiling, was grabbed by the leg and forcibly slammed down to the floor.――No, he was pulled from the floor again, thrown up to the ceiling with an upward swing, down to the floor with a downward swing. Ceiling, floor, ceiling, floor――up and down, like a child playing with a doll.


"S-Stop..."

"Begging? It's always the same with you."


His plea, mixed with blood and stomach acid, was swallowed by the impact of the sideways wind, and granted.

His entire body, beaten against floor and ceiling without exception, was finally thrown into a cracked stone wall, and that ended it.

The accumulated impacts far exceeded Heinkel's comprehension, and he couldn't possibly know what parts of his body were unharmed and what were not.

And yet, without understanding――,


"You're a man beyond reasoning."


"a, gih――!"


Marcos's falling heel crushed Heinkel's right hand by sheer force.

The back of his hand and wrist were destroyed by the hard heel, and even when he tried to pull his arm away, it wouldn't budge, as if caught between boulders. His foot twisted, and his four fingers other than the thumb made an unpleasant sound.


"gi, aaaa――!"


"Don't wail, it's unbearable to hear."


Cursed for the base nature that produced such ugly screams, Heinkel bared his teeth. He bit at Marcos's ankle to try to pry off the foot crushing his right hand. It was useless. His face was kicked by the opposite foot, and the mark of a boot was deeply engraved into his forehead.


"Give up already."


Marcos, demonstrating the overwhelming difference in power, threw that out carelessly.

"Give up"――what a foolish thing to say. His will to fight had long been scattered to the winds. In the first place, he'd never had even a shred of something as grand as fighting spirit from the moment he reluctantly agreed to cooperate with this matter.


Yes, that's right, of course it was.

Heinkel had known from the beginning that such a plan could never succeed.


"Why are you like this?"


His vision exploded in white.

His head was grabbed by the back, and his face was slammed into the floor with full force.


"You have absolutely no capacity for reflection."


He was grabbed by the collar and lifted, and while his feet dangled, a fist punched through his stomach.

The impact had nowhere to escape, and all his internal organs began a chorus of pain, as if they had burst inside his body.


"What do you want to do?"


Two hits, three hits, four hits, five hits――the impacts continued.

The great chorus was interrupted each time, becoming more pathetic each time it resumed. Even though he was being punched in the stomach, the contents of his head seemed to spill out, and he couldn't think of anything.


"What do you want to become?"


There was. There should have been. Something, there was.

Things he wanted to say, things he should do, hopes, things he couldn't throw away――something like that, there should have been, should have been.


"Tell me, Heinkel Astrea.――How many more times, how many more people, how much more, do you need to disappoint others before you're satisfied?"


The hand grasping his collar released.

Unable to support his body with his toes touching the floor, he collapsed forward, his knees and forehead striking the floor, and blood spread around Heinkel as he lay face-down.

Copious nosebleeds and vomit from his mercilessly crushed face, and his internal organs, beaten and churned over and over again, flowed out as bloody stool.


"――――"


He couldn't stand. Couldn't stand. Couldn't, stand.


"Please! Stop it already! Don't hurt Sir Heinkel any more than this!"


Bleeding from above and below, drowning in his own blood, on the verge of death by drowning――a girl's shrill scream tried to shield Heinkel.

It was terribly laughable. There was nothing here worthy of that scream, that plea.


"Lady Philoane, you are being used by this man."


"No! That's not it... That's not it at all! With Sir Heinkel, I, of my own――"


"Idiot, stop it! Don't ruin the old man's pride!"


"――gh, Felt, but still!"


Above his head as he lay collapsed and immobile, a desperate exchange was taking place.

Felt was right. Philoane was wrong. Against the "Boulder" standing in their way, the girls could never escape.

Though Reinhard was always the one talked about, Marcos was also that kind of existence.

By now, this plan's objective was no longer to meet the victory conditions, but had shifted to a perspective of how to minimize damage and beg the opponent's forgiveness.

That's why Felt was right, and Philoane was wrong.


"Stop it already, old man! He's gonna die at this rate!"


"Sir Heinkel...!"


Felt's voice, knowing what needed to be done, and Philoane's voice, unable to abandon her dreamy ideals even in this situation――both were calling to Heinkel.


Unfortunately, he had no strength left to respond to either voice. He was literally breathing his last, struggling just not to drown in his own blood and stomach acid.

In the first place, "stop it already" and "don't kill him"――the one those pleas needed to be directed at wasn't Heinkel, but Marcos, who was making Heinkel into a tattered rag.


And even Marcos――he must have been truly furious. Or perhaps he had finally reached the limit of his patience.

Heinkel had received looks of contempt from him before, but it had been a long time since he'd been physically subdued like this.

Today, at this moment, the figure of Heinkel reflected in Marcos's eyes――dragging around royal selection candidates to use them in his schemes――was wicked and convenient. Finally, he could justifiably unleash his daily――no, his years of accumulated anger.


So, to still so persistently, against a Heinkel who was now unresisting and could do nothing――,


"――What does it matter now, you damn fool."


With a click of his tongue, Marcos stepped in.

A fist was coming. The moment his consciousness registered that, the approaching fist wind struck the side of his face, and as his cheekbone was crushed, his body spun half-way around and crashed into the corridor wall again――this time the opposite one.

His embedded body was grabbed by the collar, pulled down backward, and his back was driven into a knee. The bones from his spine and hip to his ribs creaked and shattered, and he vomited blood profusely.


"o, aa――!"


His arm flailed as blood spilled, and his wrist was caught. Impact entered his straightened elbow from the outside, and white bone broke through skin and flesh from the snapped arm.


"u, a... goh"


Marcos's hand was thrust into his mouth, opened to let out a rising cry of pain.

The fist was forcibly opened inside his mouth, and with a hard sound, Heinkel's jaw was dislocated. Several back teeth were broken, and his temple and the back of his head were struck by the hammer of a fist, by elbows, again and again and again.


"――gh"


Half of his hazy vision went dark. Perhaps his eye had been crushed.

His nose was flattened, the inside of his mouth was wrecked, his arm was broken, his organs had burst――there wasn't a single place not wet with blood.


It was persistent. Not something that could be described with words like merciless or cruel.

More cruel than simply killing, more wanton than simple torture, an act that made one want to avert their eyes――had Marcos lost himself in anger? He shouldn't have been a man with such a mentality as to continue kicking the corpse of an opponent he had so one-sidedly beaten down.


And yet, why did he continue to hit, kick, and trample?

Against a Heinkel who had long since――no, from the very beginning――not the slightest will to resist――,


"――Even after all this, you still intend to draw your sword."


――.

――――.

――――――――. What?


"――――"


He couldn't understand at all what Marcos was saying.

Drawing his sword or not――not a shred of such spirit had welled up. In fact, his right hand was broken from the elbow, the wrist crushed, all fingers pointing in wrong directions.


His face had been beaten and crushed repeatedly, the right side of his vision was pitch black and saw nothing. Inside his mouth overflowing with blood, the sound of his breathing barely escaping through the gaps in his teeth was that of a dying man――surely there was no need to even question the will to fight of a man barely alive.


In that half-broken vision, he could see Marcos, splattered with blood that had flown from Heinkel, and beyond him, the two girls forced to witness the battle――the one-sided violence. One had her cheeks stiff, the other had her large eyes filled with tears, her hands clasped before her chest as if in prayer.

From their figures too, it was plainly evident that this was a scene of intolerable brutality.


And then――,


"――a?"


At a small sound that faintly vibrated his eardrums, a questioning voice leaked from his throat.

It came from Heinkel's waist, from the beloved sword hanging at the sword belt firmly wrapped there. The quiet, clear, ringing sound of a blade being drawn from its scabbard――the sound of steel gliding through the sheath――.


"――――"


His right arm broken, crushed, his face destroyed, his organs burst, made to spew bloody vomit and bloody stool――and yet, the left hand he had protected through it all had made him draw his sword.


"Ah, I see..."

What was there to it.

Indeed, Marcos was not some contemptible man who, against an opponent fallen and unable to move, would continue to pile on attacks in violation of the spirit of chivalry.


Heinkel had simply still been standing.

Still been trying to draw his sword.


"Still..."

――Still trying to play the knight, am I?



　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　△▼△▼△▼△



"――――"


The blood-stained sound of his broken nose made a foolish noise in the corridor tense with earnest tension.

Silent, but not soundless. Playing the knight, but not someone who could call himself a knight.


And yet he drew his sword. For what purpose? There was no plausible answer.

Only, somewhere beyond his broken body and hazy consciousness, he could hear something.

Not the sound of this moment.

It was――,


"――Sir Heinkel is here."


An irresponsible voice resurfaced in his head, from which his thoughts were flowing out along with his blood.

Even when threatened that she would lose everything, a foolish woman, a girl without discerning eyes, who had declared that there were things that would remain by her side――her voice remained in his head.


"――Congratulations."


He could hear a voice of congratulation.

Not sarcasm or irony, but a voice celebrating that position, that way of being.

A voice that understood what swords were drawn for, and yet was forced into the constraints of being unable to carry through with that way of being――it remained in his heart.


"――How delightful! Sir Heinkel!"


He could hear a beloved voice.

Simply distant, simply far away, simply, simply dear――a voice that felt precious remained in his soul.


His head, and heart, and soul, and――what else needed to be gathered?


"o, oo...!"


With a voiceless roar, the accumulated training ingrained in the corpse that had long since become that of the ideal――it moved Heinkel's left arm.


There was no stance, no footwork. It was a flash that couldn't be called a sword strike by any stretch――swung around by the weight of his collapsing body.

But that sword flash certainly reached Marcos's thick neck.


"――――"


Marcos's solemn face, truly befitting one called "The Boulder"――his eyes narrowed.

The sword flash reached. Marcos neither drew his sword nor deflected it with his gauntlet. The sword flash was simply blocked by the gray bedrock covering the skin of Marcos's thick neck.

A neck thick as a log, well-trained. What covered it was multiple layers of rising rock shell, and the thickly deployed armor of stone easily received the steel sword strike.


Sparks scattered.

The blade rebounded, and the impact passed through Heinkel's left arm.――On the rock shell covering Marcos's neck, only a single white line had been carved.


"It's over."


A fist pierced into Heinkel's defenseless torso after he had released the sword strike.


"――――"


He didn't even feel pain.

The moment the fist touched, his vision transformed, and the world repeated darkness and brightness. It was only after his entire body was struck by the impact, after he had slammed into the wall, leaned against it, and this time truly sunk down with his legs stretched out, that he realized it was the result of his body flying through the air in a vertical spin.


Half-embedded in the cracked wall, Heinkel's hand hung limply, and with a sharp sound, the sword gripped by his dangling left hand struck the floor powerlessly.

This time for certain――his fingers, his eyelids, his tongue, nothing would move.


"――――"


He could hear footsteps approaching――one step, two steps, three steps.

Feeling Marcos's approach as he slowly trod down the corridor, Heinkel faced the approaching moment of the end head-on, moment by moment.


It was ending. Was it ending? Would he be ended?

Could it be――Marcos, of all people? Would he be the one to close this terribly foolish life?

The feeling within him that he could never imagine finding peace from that was utterly, utterly absurd――,


"...Stop it."


He said that to the slender back that had run past Marcos and stood before him.


"No, I won't stop. There's no way I would stop."


Spreading both arms wide, the girl stood in Marcos's way, shielding Heinkel.

Her blood-drained, pale face, her cheeks wet with tears she couldn't hold back, her teeth chattering from Marcos's overwhelming presence that felt almost bestial――and yet she stood.

Philoane stood, protecting the battered Heinkel.


"Please step aside, Lady Philoane."


"N-No. No. I cannot do that. I will not move from here."


"That man is using you."


"No! You're wrong! This was all something I asked for!"


In response to Marcos's quietly advancing words, as if to rouse her own courage, Philoane raised her voice and answered back.

"Wait," "stop," "don't let her say any more"――his heart urged. But it was no use.


"I asked Sir Heinkel to lend me his strength to save Emilia and Felt, and to think of a way to take them out of the castle."


"――――"


"Sir Heinkel tried to stop me many times! He persuaded me to give up. He said I would lose my position as a royal selection candidate and my title as 'Saint,' everything! Even so!"


"――――"


"Even so, I asked him. Of Sir Heinkel.――My knight."


The more she spoke, the more the trembling disappeared from Philoane's voice.

What a simple girl. Could one really dispel fear by raising one's voice as if to rouse a frightened heart?

But in fact, Philoane straightened her back, wiped her tears, and faced her opponent squarely.


"That man is not a knight. He is a 'Sword-Bearer' who cast away his knight's qualifications himself."


Marcos was right.


"No, you're wrong. This person is my knight. A true knight, bound by oath."


Philoane's words were wrong.


"――――"


Their opinions clashed head-on, and Philoane and Marcos glared at each other.

In height, age, and ability――everything was different, everything had a gap. And yet, it was not Philoane who averted her eyes first. It was Marcos.


"Is that so."


Shortly, it had a ring like ancient rock being split by dripping water.

Having said that, Marcos slowly opened his tightly clenched fist. Then, just as he moved his lips to say something――,


"――That's enough."


A clear, silver-bell-like voice rang through the devastated corridor.



　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　　△▼△▼△▼△



"――Emilia."


It was Philoane who murmured that, dazed, turning toward the voice at the far end of the corridor.

Unfortunately, Heinkel, on the verge of death, couldn't even move his neck. However, the high sound of footsteps and the faintly felt wave of cold air confirmed the identity of the newcomer who had appeared.

Before long, even in the corner of Heinkel's vision, the girl with long silver hair――Emilia, who had opened the closed door and come this far――was reflected.

And that was――,


"Seriously, give me a break. Just slipping through and getting to the door felt like risking my life."


It was the achievement of Felt, who lined up beside Emilia while speaking with a curse.

At the same moment Philoane had rushed in to protect Heinkel, Felt had seized the gap in Marcos's consciousness and leaped to the door of the room where Emilia was.

And she had brought her out, and made her witness this battle situation.――What Emilia thought of it, he couldn't know, but.


"That's enough, Sir Marcos. Sir Heinkel has a very sturdy body, but if you do any more, he'll die. I absolutely cannot overlook that."


"Even if this man is a wretch who schemed to use your person, Lady Emilia?"


"Even if that were so, no. And besides, Philoane was just now earnestly explaining that it isn't so. Isn't that right?"


So saying, Emilia signaled Philoane with her eyes. Receiving that, Philoane, who had been dumbfounded, came to her senses and hurriedly nodded her head vigorously up and down.


"Yes, yes, that's right! That's how it is! Sir Heinkel wasn't trying to use Emilia or Felt! If anything, the mastermind is me!"


"Don't put it in a way that makes it more complicated! Anyway, the old man wasn't trying to harm us or big sis Emilia, that's the point."


"Right, that's the point!"


Emilia and Felt each took positions flanking Philoane, and with a face as if she had received the support of ten thousand soldiers, Philoane pointed her finger sharply at Marcos.

In fact, three royal selection candidates stood together. And in a formation protecting the battered Heinkel, confronting the Royal Guard Captain Marcos.

That was truly――,


"――For someone of the Royal Guard Captain's standing to be glared at by all three royal selection candidates at once, this is quite a promising sight for the future."


That voice belonged to yet another newcomer, different from the three royal selection candidates and, of course, different from Heinkel and Marcos.

The source of the footsteps was the same as Emilia――a room at the far end of the corridor. The one who had been confined in that room together with Emilia was――,


"――Lady Ram."


"You've made quite a mess, Sir Marcos. Even though I rewrote the formula for today, causing this much of a disturbance could easily be noticed by someone else. Are you in your right mind?"


"I intended to take every possible precaution, but given this state of affairs, I have no excuse."


To Marcos, who slowly shook his head, the peach-haired maid who had spoken haughtily――the elder twin sister of the girl Priscilla had favored, Ram, snorted "Hah!"

At that exchange, it was Emilia who furrowed her brow, saying "What do you mean?"


"Um, from what you're saying just now, it sounds like Ram and Sir Marcos are very good friends."


"No, that is a misunderstanding, Lady Emilia. The one who is very good friends with Sir Marcos is not Ram, but Lord Roswaal. Fifteen years of bosom friendship, apparently."


"I would like to correct that as it is damaging to my honor. It is true that we have known each other for fifteen years, but being called bosom friends harms my reputation."


"Ah, that answer might be very typical of a friend of Roswaal's..."


"W-Wait wait wait! What are you all getting chummy about all of a sudden, hey!"


At Ram and Marcos's responses, from beside Emilia who had put a finger to her lips, Felt interjected with the sensible observation about how strange the situation was.

She then pointed at Heinkel, crushed into a pulp, and,


"This rock-face was rampaging like he was trying to kill just a moment ago, you know. Thanks to that, the old man's in this state, isn't he? What the hell is going on."


"Indeed. I would like to confirm... Lady Philoane, is what you said earlier true? That you infiltrated the castle to save Lady Emilia and Lady Felt?"


"Eh? Yes, that's right! I came to save the two of them. I carefully planned for it, and we managed to successfully get Felt out, and with this momentum, we came to get Emilia too..."


"I see.――Did you think of that yourself?"


"I planned it together with Sir Heinkel. The initial idea was my own."


Placing her hand on her chest, Philoane confessed as if there was no longer anything to hide.

Rather than showing any shame, Philoane's answer seemed almost relieved to have spoken of it, and both Ram and Marcos furrowed their brows at her response.

Before those two's meaningful reactions, Philoane let out an "Um,"


"I still haven't fully grasped the situation, but... may I treat Sir Heinkel? No one will stop me, right? Although I would do it even if you tried to stop me."


"Yes, of course, please do. Heal him quickly... Ah, but healing magic might not work well here. Since magic has been disabled..."


"Hehe, it's fine, don't worry. My miracle is not magic."


So saying, Philoane crouched right before Heinkel's eyes. Feeling her gaze up close, Heinkel, unable to move, couldn't say anything.


"You don't need to say anything. Sir Heinkel's actions were the greatest proof."


――He didn't understand. What was it that Heinkel had proven?


"――――"


As Heinkel remained uncomprehending, Philoane's hand gently touched his face. From there, a soft, warm sensation gradually spread.

Indeed, it was a sensation different from healing magic.――If this was a miracle of the "Dragon God Church," then this, which brought about results different from magic, might reach what could not be reached.

Even while his own body was being healed, Heinkel found himself thinking such things.

While Heinkel and the others were thus occupied――,


"So, big sis Emilia, this margrave, and rock-face are friends, and what were you plotting with the maid?"


"You may find it hard to believe, but... today, I too visited this place intending to take Lady Emilia and Lady Felt out of the royal castle."


"...Eh!? Sir Marcos, you were going to take us?"


"Yes," Marcos nodded heavily, and Ram, hugging her own elbows, supplemented.


"Originally, I had been instructed by Lord Roswaal. He said that if something happened in the capital, I should rely on Sir Marcos at that time. That he would definitely lend his strength... So Ram accepted being detained together with Lady Emilia."


"I never explicitly said 'definitely.' It depends on the circumstances at the time. Given my position, it is also undesirable for me to favor a single royal selection candidate. However, this time the circumstances are different."


"So that means you also thought it was a situation where you had to side with us."


"That is correct. To that end, I reduced the security of this wing to minimal personnel, and to delay the discovery of the situation as much as possible..."


"Ram cooperated by rewriting the formula of the magic restricting this floor. I converted part of its effect into a formula preventing the commotion and voices here from leaking outside."


"Ahh, I see. So that's why no one came running as backup even though rock-face was beating the old man up like that."


The circumstances being explained matched with the inexplicable facts, and Felt nodded in understanding. Then, Philoane, who had been listening while concentrating on her miracle, said "W-Wait a moment?" without stopping her hands,


"Um, so that means Sir Heinkel being beaten down like that by the Captain was..."


"A pointless conflict where allies crushed each other, yes."


"I don't think so. Neither that it was a pointless conflict, nor that this man is an ally."


"――gh"


Marcos, cutting her off, still refusing to acknowledge Heinkel as sharing the same thoughts――pain ran across Philoane's profile.

However, though it was unfortunate for Philoane, it was natural for Marcos to think that way.

Heinkel's past actions were not so light that they could be overturned by a slight change in behavior.


"Sir Marcos, the fact that you prepared to take us out means you'll be coming with us too?"


"That is my intention."


"Is it fine for the Knight Captain to do that? The capital's already in chaos, right? If on top of that even the Knight Captain disappears..."


"If pus must be released by spilling blood, then bloodshed should not be shunned. Besides, this is not a knight order that would collapse from the absence of one person like myself. I believe each of them holds in their hearts how they should raise their swords."


Marcos asserted that it was already decided, with no intention of changing it.

At that answer, Emilia lowered her chin and looked at Philoane,


"Philoane, we'll go with Sir Marcos. You all..."


"Of course, I'm going with you, Emilia! That was my intention from the start, and I can't stay in the capital as it is now. Besides..."


"Besides?"


"I want to make the Knight Captain understand. That Sir Heinkel is a proper knight."


"――――"


At Philoane's spirited declaration, Marcos narrowed his eyes silently. No matter how many words were strung together, there was an accumulation of actions unworthy of belief.

Ignoring Marcos's reaction, Felt scratched her head, and Emilia smiled.


"Yes, then let's go together! Thank you, Philoane. Even though doing this would put you in tremendous trouble, you worked hard for us."


"Of course! That's only natural. After all, I'm Emilia's best friend, and with Felt, it's... what? A complicated relationship, but it's like we're sisters, isn't it! ...Like sisters! Isn't it!"


"Did you like it? Why'd you say it twice..."


With Felt's exasperated sigh, Philoane simultaneously lowered her raised hand and let out a long, long, deep breath.

Sweat on her brow, slightly out of breath, she nodded and said "Good,"


"I've managed to handle the emergency for now. Sir Heinkel, can you stand?"


"...No, sorry."


Without a mirror, he couldn't know his appearance, but at the very least, the pain in his struck head, crushed back teeth, and broken right arm had considerably subsided.

That said, the sturdiness of Heinkel's body was certified for a certain reason. How much of this was the effect of the miracle and how much was the result of his body's abnormality, he couldn't tell.

In any case, standing up would still require some more time――,


"――Time for discussion is precious, so excuse me."


So saying, Marcos walked up unceremoniously, lightly lifted Heinkel's body in his arms, and roughly slung him over his shoulder like luggage.

At that moment, the sword Heinkel had been gripping was snatched away and returned to its scabbard.


"Knight Captain... you've come to believe in Sir Heinkel!?"


"No, it merely means I can cut him down elsewhere if need be."


"Th-That would be pointless! Even if his torso were cut in two, I would put him back together with my miracle!"


"Enough! Save your arguments for later! Let's go before we're found!"


Chiding Philoane as she snapped at Marcos, who was carrying Heinkel, Emilia looked over the faces of everyone present and took the lead.

Each of them was prepared to advance into a situation from which there was no turning back through this decision. Seeing the expressions of everyone, Emilia nodded deeply in return.

And then――,


"――We need to meet up with Subaru and everyone else. They're surely doing something incredibly reckless right about now, so I'm worried!"


"Big bro would probably say he doesn't want to hear that from us escaping."


Exchanging such words, the group, now larger than either of their plans had intended, left the castle.

And so, in the midst of escaping the castle,


"Sir Heinkel is as expected. I'm so proud!"


"...My nose is broken, though."


To Philoane, who for some reason seemed proud despite having watched him be reduced to a tattered rag, Heinkel could only respond that with his immobile body.
